> """
> Provider-neutral model adapter protocol.
> 
> Adapters encapsulate provider SDKs and expose only capabilities required by
> Planner/Responder. They do not choose plans, mutate learning state, or inject
> planner-owned context.
> 
> Required adapter contract:
> 
> class ModelAdapter(Protocol):
>     def chat_response(
>         self,
>         messages: Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]],
>         max_tokens: int | None = None,
>     ) -> str: ...
> 
>     def stream_response(
>         self,
>         messages: Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]],
>         max_tokens: int | None = None,
>     ) -> Iterator[str]: ...
> 
>     def allowed(self, tokens: int) -> bool:
>         '''
>         Return False when unavailable due to context limits, quota, health,
>         policy, provider outage, or other execution constraints.
>         '''
>         ...
> 
>     def estimate_cost(
>         self,
>         prompt_tokens: int,
>         completion_tokens: int,
>     ) -> float | None: ...
> 
> Caller contract:
> - responders.py calls `adapter.allowed(estimated_prompt_tokens)` before
>   invocation;
> - responders.py calls chat_response/stream_response only after Planner's
>   context assembler has created effective messages;
> - metrics.py records actual provider usage where available;
> - no adapter should rely on a global mutable "last responder".
> """
