> How can I make the system reliably think before responding?
**assistant**:
> Your problem is not “the model won’t think.” It is that the contract currently asks for **answer-first, optional-tool-afterward behavior**, and then hopes the model will voluntarily choose research. For reliable “think before responding,” make planning a **protocol invariant**, not a prompt preference.
> 
> Key changes I’d make:
> 
> 1. **Stop saying “optional” when it is required.**
> 
> Your prompt currently says:
> 
> > “append at most one optional execution plan”  
> > “A plan is required”
> 
> That contradiction is enough for models to ignore it. Use either:
> 
> ```text
> You MUST append exactly one terminal ```plan block.
> If no external work is needed, the plan must return:
> { "action": "none", "reason": "..." }
> ```
> 
> or, better, split required vs optional modes.
> 
> 2. **For research tasks, use a plan-first responder.**
> 
> If you want the system to research before answering, don’t ask for:
> 
> ```text
> visible answer
> then optional plan
> ```
> 
> Ask for:
> 
> ```text
> private/hidden planning call → execute JS → final synthesis answer
> ```
> 
> In other words, add a responder like `JavaScriptFirstResponder`:
> 
> ```text
> model emits only a JS plan / no-op decision
> → runtime executes it
> → model writes final answer from results
> ```
> 
> For `chat_response`, the user never needs to see the preliminary answer. For streaming, withhold visible output until the planning phase completes, or stream a neutral status message only if your UX wants that.
> 
> 3. **Make absence of a plan a retryable protocol failure.**
> 
> For JS-required plans:
> 
> ```python
> visible_text, javascript_plan = extract_plan(response.text)
> 
> if javascript_plan is None and plan.metadata.get("requires_javascript_plan"):
>     # only safe before visible output
>     retry_with_stronger_protocol_prompt()
> ```
> 
> For non-streaming, this is easy. For streaming, you already have the right rule: retry only before visible output begins.
> 
> 4. **Fix your selector cue mismatch.**
> 
> `decision._cue_bonus()` checks:
> 
> ```python
> mode == "rag"
> mode == "parallel"
> mode == "direct"
> ```
> 
> but your plans use:
> 
> ```python
> "web_rag_js"
> "parallel_direct_web_js"
> "javascript_planning"
> ```
> 
> So your web/parallel plans are not getting the intended boost. Change it to match actual modes.
> 
> Also add cues for this exact class of task:
> 
> ```python
> multi_entity = many capitalized names
> people_lookup = "people", "department visit", "meeting", "seminar"
> ```
> 
> Then heavily boost `parallel_direct_web_js` or `web_rag_js`.
> 
> 5. **For multi-person lists, don’t rely on one search query.**
> 
> Your default web query is the entire user message. For this task, the right JS plan is per-person fanout:
> 
> ```javascript
> async function main(input) {
>   const people = [
>     "Jeffrey Sun University of Toronto economics",
>     "Jacquelyn Pless Rotman School of Management",
>     "Christian Spielmann University of Toronto economics",
>     "Karen Clay University of Toronto economics",
>     "Larasati Wulandari University of Toronto economics",
>     "Benjamin Lauzon University of Toronto economics",
>     "Ayaka Behro University of Toronto economics",
>     "Eduardo Souza-Rodrigues University of Toronto economics",
>     "Hugo Cordeau University of Toronto economics",
>     "Christoph Semken University of Toronto economics"
>   ];
> 
>   const results = await parallelMap(
>     people,
>     { concurrency: 4 },
>     async query => await tools["web.search"]({ query })
>   );
> 
>   return { people, results };
> }
> ```
> 
> 6. **Fix the JS execution path bugs before making plans mandatory.**
> 
> `JavaScriptPlanningResponder.chat_response()` currently has serious issues:
> 
> ```python
> outcome = self._execute_plan(..., initial_text)
> ```
> 
> but `initial_text` is undefined; you probably mean `visible_text`.
> 
> Then this block references undefined variables:
> 
> ```python
> artifact_id = self._save_plan_result(
>     plan=plan,
>     record=record,
>     run=run,
>     result=result,
> )
> ```
> 
> Remove that duplicate save; `_execute_plan()` already saves result/failure artifacts.
> 
> 7. **Change the protocol from “think” to “decide and act.”**
> 
> A robust prompt fragment:
> 
> ```text
> For this execution mode, you must not answer substantively until external
> evidence has been gathered when the request involves current facts, named
> people, organizations, citations, or multiple entities.
> 
> Append exactly one terminal ```plan block.
> 
> If research is needed, the plan must call tools and return evidence.
> If research is not needed, the plan must return:
> { "action": "none", "reason": "..." }
> 
> Do not provide the final answer before the plan.
> ```
